  <span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden"><h2  class="h2">Daily activities and demonstrations</h2>
</span>





  
      <div class="field field--name-field-paragraphs field--type-entity-reference-revisions field--label-hidden field__items">
              <div class="field__item">  <div class="paragraph paragraph--type--fixed-layout paragraph--view-mode--default">
                  
                          
                                  
                  <div class="toc-selectors layout layout--bootstrap-fixed-grid-row-1 d-flex flex-wrap">

            
              
                                                                                      <div  class="layout__region layout__region--main col-12">
                          
                                                      <div class="paragraph paragraph--type--text-block paragraph--view-mode--default">
          
            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>Step back in time at Ottawa’s very own living history museum! Experience rural life in a recreated 1920s and 30s village. Chat with costumed villagers as they complete daily tasks on the farm, in the home, or at work. Explore the General Store or a one-room Schoolhouse. Get a glimpse at domestic life as you move between Duford House and Foubert House. Check out a trade demonstration highlighting authentic tools and techniques of the era. Learn about life on the rails in the CN Caboose, see a 1927 firetruck in the Fire Hall, take a quiet moment in Knox Church and discover a piece of local transportation history at Watson’s Garage. Don’t forget to say hello to the heritage breed animals that call the museum home each summer!</p>
<p>Activities and demonstrations are offered <strong>Wednesday to Sunday between 9 am and 3 pm</strong>, <strong>excluding special event days</strong> when themed programming is delivered. For information about special events, visit <a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/place-listing/cumberland-heritage-village-museum">ottawa.ca/cumberlandmuseum</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Activities and demonstrations rotate throughout the week. Be sure to ask on arrival about the day’s highlights!&nbsp;</strong></p>
<p>*Activities and demonstrations may be adjusted or cancelled in the event of unsafe weather conditions or other unforeseen circumstances. Thank you for your understanding.&nbsp;</p>
<h4>Tractor-pulled wagon rides</h4>
<p>Take a tour of the village in a tractor-pulled accessible wagon. Meet the wagon at Watson’s Garage to join the tour: <strong>10 am&nbsp;</strong>and <strong>1 pm.</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<p>*Due to the increased number of pedestrian visitors on the village paths during large events, wagon rides are not offered on these days. Thank you for helping us keep all our visitors safe. To learn more about special events, visit ottawa.ca/cumberlandmuseum.&nbsp;</p>
<h4>Heritage trades and skills</h4>
<p>Heritage trade and skill demonstrations rotate from Wednesday to Saturday. <strong>They may include</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Blacksmithing</li>
<li>Carpentry and woodworking</li>
<li>Food preparation and preservation (cooking, baking, etc.)</li>
<li>Gardening and farming</li>
<li>Leatherworking</li>
<li>Mechanics (machinery, vehicle and equipment maintenance)</li>
<li>Milling (sawmill)</li>
<li>Printing and typesetting</li>
<li>Textile arts (sewing, quilting, embroidery, etc.)</li>
<li>Tinsmithing&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<h4>Sundays at the museum</h4>
<p>On Sundays, activities and demonstrations shift to exploring themes of leisure time and social gatherings. Activities and demonstrations rotate from week to week. <strong>They may include</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>Movies, radio shows or music from the era</li>
<li>Food preparation and preservation</li>
<li>Gardening and harvesting</li>
<li>Heritage trades</li>
<li>Community needlework projects (sewing bee, quilting bee, etc.)</li>
</ul>
<h4>Canteen and Boutique</h4>
<p>Please note that the canteen is temporarily closed as we complete renovations. Chocolate bars, water and pop are available for purchase at the admission desk (Train Sation): <strong>9 am to 4 pm.</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Visitors are always welcome to pack snacks or a lunch from home to enjoy a picnic on the village green.&nbsp;</strong></p>
<p>Browse the Boutique located in the Train Station to discover a variety of souvenirs crafted with care by the museum’s tradespeople and artisans: <strong>9 am to 4 pm.&nbsp;</strong></p></div>
      
