            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><h3><span>Murder Mystery Brunch</span></h3>
<p>Sunday, August 23 from 10:30 am to 1 pm<br>Ages 14 and up<br>Cost: $51.48 per person (plus tax). Brunch is included in the ticket price.<br><a href="https://anc.ca.apm.activecommunities.com/ottawa/activity/search/detail/194361?onlineSiteId=0&amp;locale=en-US&amp;from_original_cui=true">Advance registration is required.</a></p>
<p>Unleash your inner detective and solve the case!&nbsp;Enjoy an unforgettable morning of intrigue and suspense at&nbsp;Cumberland&nbsp;Heritage Village Museum. You will be guided through the village from scene to scene while actors bring an original murder mystery play to life. Work together to&nbsp;connect the clues and solve the case&nbsp;before time runs out.&nbsp;&nbsp;A&nbsp;seated&nbsp;buffet-style brunch, featuring a menu of classic and delicious breakfast foods, will be served mid-performance.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>“1926, the 100<sup>th</sup>&nbsp;anniversary of Bytown”</strong>&nbsp;(performed by Vintage Stock Theatre):&nbsp;It’s&nbsp;1926, and Cumberland is joining in the&nbsp;festivities for&nbsp;Ottawa’s centenary, marking the anniversary of&nbsp;Bytown’s founding. The excitement is already palpable when the Stampede Centenary Cup rolls&nbsp;through town on its way to the city for a week of rodeo entertainment. When the celebration gets too wild, the party comes to a sudden halt. A murder has taken place! And&nbsp;everyone’s&nbsp;a suspect with something to hide.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<h4><span>Notes</span></h4>
<ul>
<li><span>The performance is delivered in English.</span></li>
<li><span><strong>The performance starts promptly at 10:30 am</strong>, please plan your arrival time accordingly. Brunch will be served mid-performance at 11:30 am.&nbsp;</span></li>
<li><span>This performance involves moving between multiple outdoor locations which may include crossing gravel, grassy, or uneven terrain. Dress for weather conditions, with appropriate footwear for periods of standing or walking. Brunch will be served under a shelter with tables and seating provided.&nbsp;</span></li>
<li><span>This program runs rain or shine. A rain location at the museum has been identified in the event of inclement weather.&nbsp;</span></li>
<li><span>If you have questions or concerns regarding accessibility, contact the museum at 613-580- 2988 or </span><a href="mailto:museecumberlandmuseum@ottawa.ca"><span>museecumberlandmuseum@ottawa.ca</span></a><span>. Additional </span><a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/place-listing/cumberland-heritage-village-museum#section-432adac3-9948-4810-92c9-13811772e640"><span>information regarding accessibility</span></a><span> is available on the museum webpage. &nbsp;</span><br>&nbsp;</li>
</ul></div>
      
