            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><h3>1930s Fair Day&nbsp;</h3>
<p><strong>Date: </strong>Sunday, August 30, 2026&nbsp;<br><strong>Time:</strong> 10 am to 3 pm&nbsp;<br><strong>Cost:</strong> Adult - $9.42; Senior (ages 65 and up) - $6.65; Student (valid full-time student ID required) - $6.65; Youth (ages 6 to 17) - $6.65; Child (ages 5 and under) - Free; Family (Up to two adults, and accompanying children, all living in the same household) - $23.83. &nbsp;</p>
<p>Join us at Cumberland Heritage Village Museum for fun, games and music inspired by the history of rural fairs and community gatherings! Explore a 1920s and 30s heritage village. Test your skills with an old-fashioned midway game. Catch an ice cream making demonstration (and try a sample, while supplies last). Don’t forget your dancing shoes! Enjoy folktales with our guest storyteller and tap your feet along to authentic vintage records that will evoke the dances and radio playlists of the era. See farm animals and learn about the long tradition of livestock judging competitions. Watch artisans highlight their traditional trades. Bonus! Check out the Ottawa Valley Live Steamers and Model Engineers and participate in a hands-on demonstration of their large-scale model locomotives. &nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Special guests:</strong></p>
<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Western Russell 4-H<br>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <span>É</span>tienne Laliberté (Heritage Livestock Club of Eastern Ontario)<br>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Louis Mercier (Storyteller) - <strong>11 am and 12:30 pm</strong><br>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;DJ Hokum (Music)<br>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ottawa Olde Forge Rug Hooking<br>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Outaouais Wood Carvers<br>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Hoofbeats and Heartbeats Equine - <strong>10:30 am to 2:30 pm</strong><br>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Ottawa Valley Live Steamers and Model Engineers - <strong>10:30 am to 3 pm</strong></p>
<h4>Notes</h4>
<ul>
<li>Admission for this event is paid at the door. Please enter the museum through the Train Station (adjacent to the main parking lot).</li>
<li>This event takes place rain or shine. Please dress for weather conditions, including proper footwear for uneven, grassy or gravel terrain. Activities and demonstrations may be adjusted in the event of inclement weather.</li>
<li>There are packed gravel pathways between buildings, however some activities may take place on the lawn. If you have questions or concerns regarding accessibility, please contact the museum at 613-580-2988 or by email at <a href="mailto:undefined">museecumberlandmuseum@ottawa.ca.</a> Additional information about accessibility can be found on the <a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/recreation-and-parks/facilities/place-listing/cumberland-heritage-village-museum#section-432adac3-9948-4810-92c9-13811772e640">museum webpage</a>.</li>
