            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><h3>50<sup>th</sup> Anniversary Open House</h3>
<p>Date: Sunday, September 20, 2026<br>Time: 10 am to 3 pm<br>Cost: Free admission</p>
<p>We’re celebrating the museum’s 50<sup>th</sup> anniversary (1976-2026) with an open house! Enjoy free admission all day on Sunday, September 20. As Ottawa’s very own living history museum, Cumberland Heritage Village Museum&nbsp;offers visitors an opportunity to step back in time to experience rural life in a recreated 1920s and 30s village. Explore heritage and true-to-era homes and workshops. Browse the General Store, swing by the Firehall, or peek inside Watson’s Garage. Chat with costumed visitors, meet farm animals and watch a skilled interpreter demonstrating their trade, handicraft or even a historic recipe. See vintage machinery and equipment still in operation today or catch a ride on a tractor-pulled wagon.&nbsp;</p>
<h4>Memory Wall</h4>
<p>Drop into the Community Hall (Loyal Orange Lodge) to see the new Memory Wall featuring photographs of the museum from the last five decades, including images from the museum’s archive and submissions from community members. The Memory Wall will be on display to the public from September 20, 2026 through 2028.&nbsp;</p></div>
      
